                    <h2 id="platform-messaging-settings-PUTapi-v1-admin-messaging--channel-">Save the provider and its credentials.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>A blank secret MEANS "leave it alone". Without that rule, opening this
screen to correct a host name and saving would wipe the password, and
every clinic on the platform would stop sending at once.</p>

<span id="example-requests-PUTapi-v1-admin-messaging--channel-">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request PUT \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/admin/messaging/architecto" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"provider_key\": \"architecto\",
    \"credentials\": [
        \"n\"
    ]
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/admin/messaging/architecto"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "provider_key": "architecto",
    "credentials": [
        "n"
    ]
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "PUT",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

