                    <h2 id="tenant-billing-GETapi-v1-tenant-invoices-summary">The figures above the list: the four cards, and a count on every tab.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>The COUNTS follow the filters on screen — search, dates, type — so a
tab never promises twelve bills and opens on three. The CARDS do not:
they are the register as a whole, this month against last, which is
what somebody glancing at the top of the page is asking.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-v1-tenant-invoices-summary">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tenant/invoices/summary" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json"</code></pre></div>


