                    <h2 id="tenant-communications-automation-PUTapi-v1-tenant-communication--channel--connection">The connection itself — what patients see this arriving from.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p><code>communication.manage</code>, not <code>.view</code>: changing the number a clinic
messages from is an organisation decision, not a branch one.</p>

<span id="example-requests-PUTapi-v1-tenant-communication--channel--connection">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request PUT \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tenant/communication/architecto/connection" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"display_name\": \"b\",
    \"handle\": \"n\",
    \"provider\": \"g\",
    \"is_connected\": false,
    \"is_verified\": true,
    \"webhook_configured\": true
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tenant/communication/architecto/connection"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "display_name": "b",
    "handle": "n",
    "provider": "g",
    "is_connected": false,
    "is_verified": true,
    "webhook_configured": true
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "PUT",
    headers,
