                    <h2 id="tenant-devices-push-POSTapi-v1-tenant-communication-push-send">A notification to one person, typed here rather than from a template.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Only to somebody in this clinic with a live phone, and only while the
channel is switched on — unless it is the sender's own phone, which is
how somebody checks the wiring before switching it on. Logged as a test
so it never counts towards the channel's figures.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-v1-tenant-communication-push-send">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tenant/communication/push/send" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"user_id\": 16,
    \"title\": \"n\",
    \"body\": \"g\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tenant/communication/push/send"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "user_id": 16,
    "title": "n",
    "body": "g"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

